Human–computer interaction and accessibility (@humancomputer-interaction-and-accessibility: 0, is #chapter, #outline) { r_2R0W9QE27GX3A4YV9KMETSAE7S
Human–computer interaction studies how people understand and use digital systems. This material connects perception, interaction design, usability, accessibility, assistive technologies, user research, and evaluation, helping scientific and technical tools accommodate diverse bodies, abilities, practices, and contexts of work.

**Common preparation developed:** the [human-use and trust review](../core/Review-human-intent-authority-accessible-evidence-and-recovery.lingua) connects tasks, pending/unknown/confirmed evidence, accessible interaction contracts, error/recovery and an explicit evaluation plan. Finite model checks are distinguished from actual participant evidence and platform accessibility. Full user research, interaction design and accessibility implementation/evaluation remain pending.

**Parent:** [Computing — representation, algorithms and working systems](../Computing.lingua#r_02FE84C805C79A9D396F478641).
} r_2R0W9QE27GX3A4YV9KMETSAE7S
